      "bounded_findings": [
        "The plan explicitly names Quebrada Lampian, Quebrada Callantama, Quebrada Muyopunco (Muyucunto), Quebrada Carnay and Quebrada Lomo Largo as local watercourses or ravines in the district.",
        "The plan identifies critical sectors and field visits tied to named ravines, including Toma Huandaro-Rumoj on Quebrada Lampian, Callantama on Quebrada Callantama and Huachupampa on Quebrada Carnay.",
        "Within the same plan, Marcayjo nomenclature is internally inconsistent: a critical-point table labels Quebrada Marcayjo while later sector text and field-visit captions bind Marcayjo to Quebrada Lampian.",
        "A proposed intervention describes canalizing Quebrada Carnay to a meeting point with Quebrada Lampian at Huachupampa; this is works/topology context, not an exact reproducible confluence geometry."
      ],
      "forbidden_inferences": [
        "A critical point or proposed intervention is not an observed event footprint.",
        "Critical-point coordinates are not catchment polygons or outlets.",
        "The Marcayjo naming conflict cannot be resolved by choosing one label without independent hydrologic evidence.",
        "A planned canalization or stated meeting point does not define routing time, attenuation, discharge or hydraulic capacity.",
        "District boundaries do not define the Lampian hydrologic parent or any child catchment."
      ]
    }
  ],
